    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5652f238_285a303e",
        "filename": "test/usb_tcpmv2_td_pd_src3_e7.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1527433
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-06T19:17:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think PD_EXT_SOURCE_CAP is an extended message which we could send in response to the Get_Source_Cap_Extended control message. So, that struct doesn\u0027t actually have a field where assigning PD_EXT_SOURCE_CAP makes sense, which is what\u0027s leading to the error.\n\nThis part of the test is checking that the PD messages we send are expected. After adding the Get_Revision control message to the end of source and sink startup, I had to add Get_Revision to the group of possible tx messages in these tests. We are probably intending to check that the Source_Capabilities data message is sent, but checking for the Source_Capabilities_Extended type here happens to work because it is also 7.",
